// SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only

// The contract between scrim and an out-of-process store or notifier plugin,
// design D17 and docs/plugins.md.
//
// Transport: gRPC over one end of a socketpair scrim creates and the plugin
// inherits as file descriptor 3 (SCRIM_PLUGIN_FD names it), the same shape
// as the data plane boundary (D12). The plugin is the gRPC server; scrim is
// the only client. Nothing else can reach the socket. stdin and stdout are
// /dev/null; stderr is relayed into scrim's scrubbing log. The plugin exits
// when the socket closes.
//
// Lifecycle: Handshake first, then Configure, then the kind's own service.
// ValidateConfig is called on a separate, short-lived process during
// configuration loading and never carries credential values.
//
// Versioning: every top-level message carries `protocol` as field 1. Each side
// refuses a message whose protocol differs from its own (status
// FAILED_PRECONDITION), and scrim refuses a plugin whose Handshake reports a
// different one. Adding a field or an optional call is compatible. A change
// an older peer would misread bumps PROTOCOL_VERSION_CURRENT.
//
// Errors: a store call fails with a gRPC status whose code is the error kind:
// NOT_FOUND, PERMISSION_DENIED, UNIMPLEMENTED (operation outside the declared
// capabilities, or a value the store cannot hold byte for byte), UNAVAILABLE,
// ALREADY_EXISTS (create-only write of an existing secret), FAILED_PRECONDITION
// (store locked) and INVALID_ARGUMENT (reference or selector the plugin cannot
// honour). Any other code is read as UNAVAILABLE. scrim never prints, logs or
// returns the status message, because a store's message can echo request
// data; a plugin that wants to explain logs to stderr.
//
// Secrets: Field.value and ConfigureRequest.secrets are the only fields that
// hold secret material. Neither side may log them, echo them in a status, or
// keep them past the call except where the call's purpose is to store them.

